      "content": "The propagation of DNS changes can take anywhere from a few minutes to up to 72 hours, because recursive DNS servers around the world need time to update their cached records from their authoritative source. Depending on their TTL (time to live) settings, the new IP address might not appear immediately. If the TTL was set to a shorter period, the change will propagate faster, but in general, it's normal to wait for some time.",
