    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so it's basically just caching lag then? i was worried something actually went wrong with the records themselves or like some kind of error in the transmission. is there any way to force it to update faster or do i just have to sit here and wait?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, it's not about something going wrong with the records or an error in transmission. It's mainly due to the caching mechanism used by DNS servers. While you can't directly force the update, you can lower the Time to Live (TTL) value of your A records before making a change, so other servers will fetch the latest records quicker once the change propagates beyond your DNS zone. This way, if you frequently need updates, setting a lower TTL can help reduce waiting times.",
